From 519ee751897a16a699d626759b2f4126c333c0ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "shine.liu" <shine.liu@rock-chips.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 09:07:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix[mpp]: Skip empty extra packet in cache

An empty extra packet (length == 0) fails the capacity check
(capacity 0 < length 0 is false), so the cache buffer is never
allocated and mExtraPacket stays NULL. The memcpy below then
dereferences the NULL dst_impl and kills the working thread, so
no work is ever returned and VTS DecodeTestEmptyBuffersInserted
times out after 8s.

Ignore an incoming extra packet when no cache buffer exists yet
and it carries nothing to store.

Change-Id: I8a26b57ad26eb4ce20fc617fdb0e8eb9db9a6dbc
Signed-off-by: shine.liu <shine.liu@rock-chips.com>
---
 mpp/mpp.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mpp/mpp.c b/mpp/mpp.c
index 272ee0678..f3c306b87 100644
--- a/mpp/mpp.c
+++ b/mpp/mpp.c
@@ -54,6 +54,12 @@ static MPP_RET mpp_cache_extra_packet(Mpp *mpp, MppPacket src)
     size_t capacity = dst_impl ? dst_impl->size : 0;
     MPP_RET ret;
 
+    /* No cache buffer allocated and nothing to store: the incoming extra
+     * packet is empty (length == 0). Just ignore it, otherwise the NULL
+     * dst_impl would be dereferenced below. */
+    if (!dst_impl && !src_length)
+        return MPP_OK;
+
     if (capacity < length) {
         void *data;
 
